.Dd September 1, 2026
.Dt OCIFBSD-CLUSTER 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ocifbsd-cluster
.Nd run an ocifbsd cluster node (gossip membership and Raft consensus)
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl p Ar port
.Op Fl P Ar host@ip
.Op Fl s Ar statefile
.Op Fl n Ar name
.Op Fl i Ar interval
.Cm run
.Nm
.Fl h | Fl v
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
runs a single node of an ocifbsd cluster.
Nodes discover one another through a UDP gossip protocol with SWIM-style
failure detection, and agree on a replicated log through the Raft consensus
algorithm: leader election, log replication with commit on a quorum,
crash-durable persistence, dynamic membership, and log compaction with
snapshots.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width ".Fl i Ar interval"
.It Fl p , Fl Fl port Ar port
UDP port for gossip and consensus traffic.
The default is 6789.
All nodes in a cluster must use the same port.
.It Fl P , Fl Fl peer Ar host@ip
A seed peer, given as its node name and reachable IP address
.Pq for example Ar db1@192.0.2.11 .
Repeat for each seed peer.
A newly started node announces itself to its seed peers, so a running cluster
learns of it automatically.
.It Fl s , Fl Fl state Ar statefile
Path to the Raft state file.
When set, the current term, the vote, and the log are persisted here so the
node recovers its state across a restart; when unset, state is kept only in
memory.
.It Fl n , Fl Fl name Ar name
Override this node's identifier.
The default is the host's name.
.It Fl i , Fl Fl interval Ar interval
Print a status line every
.Ar interval
seconds.
The default is 0, which prints only when the role, term, or leader changes.
.El
.Pp
The
.Cm run
operand starts the node and runs until it receives
.Dv SIGINT
or
.Dv SIGTERM .
Sending
.Dv SIGINFO
.Pq Ic Ctrl-T
prints the node's current status on demand.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Start a three-node cluster, one command per host, all on the default port with
persistent state:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# on n1 (192.0.2.10)
ocifbsd-cluster -s /var/db/ocifbsd/raft \e
    -P n2@192.0.2.11 -P n3@192.0.2.12 run

# on n2 (192.0.2.11)
ocifbsd-cluster -s /var/db/ocifbsd/raft \e
    -P n1@192.0.2.10 -P n3@192.0.2.12 run

# on n3 (192.0.2.12)
ocifbsd-cluster -s /var/db/ocifbsd/raft \e
    -P n1@192.0.2.10 -P n2@192.0.2.11 run
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ocifbsd 8
.Sh AUTHORS
This software was developed by
.An REVYTECH, Inc.
.Sh SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
Cluster traffic is carried over UDP on the configured port; restrict that port
to the trusted cluster network with the host firewall.
Raft state files contain the replicated log and should be readable only by the
account that runs the node.
